\caption(The one-step linear model predicts zero residual but the actual nonlinear residual remains one quarter.)
\alttext(A residual parabola and its tangent show the mismatch at parameter one and a half. The second panel plots parameter states converging to square root of two. The table retains current SSE, gradient, incoming step, proposed next step and predicted SSE.)

> Checking the theory

>> Compare exact quadratic and linear error recurrences

For the zero-residual square-root fit, the iteration is
\(p_{k+1}=(p_k+2/p_k)/2\). With \(e_k=p_k-\sqrt2\), direct algebra gives
\(e_{k+1}=e_k^2/(2p_k)\): the error is quadratic until rounding dominates.

For a nonzero-residual example, fit model values \((p,p^2)\) at coordinates \((0,1)\)
to observations \((0,1)\). The objective is \(S=p^2+(p^2-1)^2\), whose positive
minimum is \(p_*=1/\sqrt2\) with \(S_*=3/4\). Its Jacobian is \((1,2p)^T\), and

$$
 p_{k+1}=p_k-\frac{p_k(2p_k^2-1)}{1+4p_k^2},\qquad
 J_*^TJ_*=3,\quad C_*=-1,\quad T'(p_*)=\frac13.
$$
\alttext(The nonzero-residual scalar update subtracts p times two p squared minus one, divided by one plus four p squared. At the positive solution the Jacobian squared norm is three and the residual curvature term is minus one, giving a limiting error ratio of one third.)

Both fits use exact derivatives and start at one. The first plot floors absolute
parameter errors at 1e-16 only for logarithmic display. The second shows the nonzero
case's observed error ratio before subtraction of nearly equal floating-point
numbers makes that ratio unreliable. The native trace and printed errors are kept
unfloored. These examples test explicit recurrences; they do not establish the rate
for every nonlinear fit.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/gn_local_rates.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  const auto square   = [](const std::vector<double>& p, double) { return p[0] * p[0]; };
  const auto square_j = [](const std::vector<double>& p, double) {
    return std::vector<double>{2 * p[0]};
  };
  const auto curved = [](const std::vector<double>& p, double x) {
    return x == 0 ? p[0] : p[0] * p[0];
  };
  const auto curved_j = [](const std::vector<double>& p, double x) {
    return std::vector<double>{x == 0 ? 1 : 2 * p[0]};
  };
  const auto zero = dm::algorithms::gauss_newton(square, square_j, {0}, {2}, {1}, 30, 1e-14);
  const auto nonzero =
      dm::algorithms::gauss_newton(curved, curved_j, {0, 1}, {0, 1}, {1}, 40, 1e-14);
  auto left = dm::graphics::RPlot::create(), right = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  dm::dstruct::DataFrame                                      table;
  const std::vector<const dm::algorithms::GaussNewtonResult*> fits = {&zero, &nonzero};
  const std::vector<double>            roots                       = {std::sqrt(2.), std::sqrt(.5)};
  const std::vector<std::string>       labels = {"zero residual", "nonzero residual"};
  const std::vector<dm::graphics::RGB> colors = {{37, 99, 235}, {220, 38, 38}};
  for (std::size_t j = 0; j < 2; ++j) {
    std::vector<double>      iteration, error, logerror;
    std::vector<std::string> name;
    for (const auto& row : fits[j]->history) {
      iteration.push_back(row.iteration);
      error.push_back(std::abs(row.params[0] - roots[j]));
      logerror.push_back(std::log10(std::max(1e-16, error.back())));
      name.push_back(labels[j]);
    }
    left.line(iteration, logerror, labels[j], colors[j]);
    dm::dstruct::DataFrame rows;
    rows.add_column("problem", name);
    rows.add_column("iteration", iteration);
    rows.add_column("absolute_error", error);
    table = table.ncols() ? table.concat_rows(rows.head(6)) : rows.head(6);
    if (j == 1) {
      std::vector<double> steps, ratios;
      for (std::size_t i = 0; i + 1 < error.size() && i < 11; ++i) {
        steps.push_back(i);
        ratios.push_back(error[i + 1] / error[i]);
      }
      right.points(steps, ratios, "observed ratio", colors[j], 5)
          .line({0, 10}, {1. / 3, 1. / 3}, "limit 1/3", {100, 116, 139});
    }
  }
  left.title("Two local error rates")
      .x_label("completed updates")
      .y_label("log10 absolute error, floor -16")
      .y_limits(-16, 2);
  right.title("Nonzero residual: ratio approaches 1/3")
      .x_label("update k to k+1")
      .y_label("absolute error ratio")
      .y_limits(.25, .65);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2).add(left).add(right).size(1100, 490).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/gn_local_rates.svg");
  dm::dstruct::DataFrame::MarkdownOptions fmt;
  fmt.digits     = 9;
  fmt.scientific = {"absolute_error"};
  std::print(
      "First six raw errors for each problem:\n\n{}\n\nNonzero-residual final state:\n\n{}\n",
      table.to_md(fmt),
      nonzero.trace().tail(1).to_md(10));
}
```
